-- title:
--   Finiteness of p^k-torsion of J₀(N) from the point count
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and a natural number $p$ that is prime. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of the elements of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, itself the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $N$; and let `JZero N` be $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, F)$, the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors, i.e. finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on the places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, by the subgroup of principal divisors. Write $g$ for `genusFF`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor. The hypothesis is the counting statement `CardinalityAJ`: for every $n$, the subtype of elements $x$ of `JZero N` with $p^n \cdot x = 0$ has cardinality exactly $p^{2gn}$. The conclusion is that for every natural number $k$ the subgroup `Pic0.torsion` of elements killed by the integer $p^k$ is finite.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the $p^k$-torsion of the Jacobian $J_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, here extracted from the hypothesised count $\#J[p^n] = p^{2gn}$ rather than proved geometrically. It supplies the finiteness needed to treat the $p$-power torsion of $J_0(N)$ as a finite Hecke- and Galois-module in the construction of the representations attached to eigenforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZero_finite_torsion_pow_of_cardinalityAJ.lean

